WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.402
John plugs it in, and
Steve presses the button.

2
00:00:08.402 --> 00:00:13.200
The Core wakes and opens a
Wi-Fi network of its own.

3
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.567
Sally joins the network the Core opened
from her phone's Wi-Fi settings.

4
00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:21.500
Next she chooses the home network.

5
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.396
Sally greets Juniper, the
agent the family named.

6
00:00:25.396 --> 00:00:29.470
The answer comes from the
Core in the Study downstairs.

7
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.635
<v Juniper>Good morning, Sally. Juniper here.

8
00:00:31.635 --> 00:00:32.950
<v Juniper>What first?

9
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.647
When Steve cancelled
his cloud gaming plan,

10
00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:39.866
his library stayed put
on his Valve account.

11
00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:44.900
Steam Headless now runs the
session on the Core in the Study.

12
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:50.832
Three years of Jean's school notes
leave a hosted notes app for Obsidian.

13
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:54.850
They are plain Markdown
files on the Core now.

14
00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:58.865
Juniper drafts three
follow-ups in the client's

15
00:00:58.865 --> 00:01:02.088
record in Twenty, and
Sally reads each one.

16
00:01:02.088 --> 00:01:06.020
The record sits on the
Core, not in a hosted CRM.

17
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.700
<v Juniper>Drafted. Please read each first.

18
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.278
John's last laptop died with a
side project's only copy on it.

19
00:01:14.278 --> 00:01:20.600
Code Server puts VS Code in a browser
tab, with the files on the Core.

20
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.397
Client records, code,
music and homework run on

21
00:01:24.397 --> 00:01:28.500
one Companion Core, in a
cottage with two studies.

22
00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:35.094
Your client records, code and family music
can run on a Companion Core at home.

23
00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:39.186
Browse the Companion Hub store
and pick your first apps.

24
00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:41.150
UnCloud your life.
